# OpenKey

STOP. Your knowledge of OpenKey may be outdated. Retrieve current facts before you write a base URL, a header or a model id.

## Retrieve first

- Docs index: https://openkey.ai/llms.txt
- Docs pages: https://openkey.ai/docs/quickstart, https://openkey.ai/docs/compatibility, https://openkey.ai/docs/errors
- Live model ids (free, no key): `GET https://api.openkey.ai/v1/models`
- Schemas: https://openkey.ai/openapi/openkey.yaml

## Three dialects, one host

| Client | Base URL | Key header |
|---|---|---|
| OpenAI SDK | `https://api.openkey.ai/v1` | `Authorization: Bearer $OPENKEY_API_KEY` |
| Anthropic SDK | `https://api.openkey.ai` (no `/v1`) | `x-api-key: $OPENKEY_API_KEY` |
| Gemini HTTP | `https://api.openkey.ai` | `x-goog-api-key: $OPENKEY_API_KEY` |

## Rules

1. The key lives only in the environment. Code reads `OPENKEY_API_KEY`; never write a key into any file. In TypeScript, check the variable before building the client.
2. No key in browser code. Call OpenKey from a server route.
3. Model ids are `provider/model`. Confirm each against the live catalog; never guess a prefix.
4. Install no OpenKey SDK. Reuse the project's OpenAI, Anthropic or Gemini client, or plain HTTP.
5. Use only `https://api.openkey.ai`. Tolerate unknown `X-OpenKey-Warning` codes.

